module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.KoszulAdicCompletionLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalSectionsKoszulDerivedLimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSmul.Coherence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.Basic

/-!
# The derived completion of a coherent module is a derived limit of its adic quotients

Let `Y` be a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_Y` be the quasi-coherent sheaf
of ideals generated by global sections `f_1, …, f_r` and let `ℱ` be a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module.
Then

`ℱ^∧ = R lim ℱ/ℐⁿℱ`,

the derived completion of `ℱ` along `ℐ` being a derived limit of the tower of adic quotients
placed in degree zero.

This is what the two halves of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] say together, in the one shape a consumer of
the identity `RΓ(U, ℱ)^∧ = R lim RΓ(U, ℱ/Iⁿℱ)` can use: part (3) identifies `ℱ^∧` with the
*ordinary* limit `lim ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` and part (4) identifies that ordinary limit with the derived one, so
`ℱ^∧` itself satisfies `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit` for the quotient tower.
Neither half alone says that: part (4) is about the ordinary limit and part (3) is an
isomorphism of objects.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.isCoherent_adicQuotientSystem_obj` — every term `ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` of the adic
  quotient tower of a coherent module on a locally Noetherian scheme is coherent.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_adicQuotientSystem_completion` — **the displayed
  statement.**

## Implementation notes

The transport of `IsDerivedLimit` from the ordinary limit to `ℱ^∧` along the isomorphism of part
(3) is `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit.of_isoObj`. The product instance is
existentially quantified exactly as in part (4), because it is produced there rather than
assumed; it is restated in the quotient-tower spelling before the transport, since the
`HasProduct` argument of `IsDerivedLimit` and the tower inside it have to be the same term for
the transport to apply.

Coherence of the terms of the tower is the one input beyond the two halves of the tag:
`ℐⁿℱ` is a quasi-coherent submodule of the coherent `ℱ` (`idealPowerMultiple_isQuasicoherent`),
hence coherent on a locally Noetherian scheme by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSmul.isCoherent_of_isQuasicoherent_submodule`, and a
cokernel of coherent modules is coherent by [Stacks, Tag 01BY] (3).

The derived category is taken with `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard` at a raised
instance priority. Both halves of the tag are stated with that instance, but the module category
appears here in two spellings — `Y.Modules` and the sheaves of modules on the ringed site of
opens of `Y` — and at the default priority the search for the derived category of the second one
picks a different instance than the one the statements of the tag carry.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe u

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.submoduleCompleteLattice

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance] modulesEnoughInjectives
attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **Every quotient `ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` of a coherent module by a power of a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals
is coherent**, on a locally Noetherian scheme. The submodule `ℐⁿℱ` is quasi-coherent, hence
coherent as a quasi-coherent submodule of a coherent module, and the quotient of coherent modules
by a coherent submodule is coherent by [Stacks, Tag 01BY] (3). -/
public theorem isCoherent_adicQuotientSystem_obj {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent] (n : ℕᵒᵖ) :
    ((adicQuotientSystem I F).obj n).IsCoherent := by
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent F
  have : (idealPowerMultiple I n.unop F).toSheafOfModules.IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSmul.isCoherent_of_isQuasicoherent_submodule F
      (idealPowerMultiple I n.unop F) (idealPowerMultiple_isQuasicoherent I n.unop F)
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_cokernel
    (idealPowerMultiple I n.unop F).ι

section Main

open scoped IsMulCommutative


variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [CompactSpace Y] {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))
  (ℱ : Y.Modules) [ℱ.IsCoherent]

/-- **The derived completion of a coherent module is a derived limit of its adic quotients.** Let
`Y` be a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme, let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_Y` be the quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals generated by the global sections `f_1, …, f_r` and let `ℱ` be a coherent `𝒪_Y`-module.
Then `ℱ^∧`, the derived completion of `ℱ` along `ℐ`, is a derived limit of the tower
`n ↦ ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` placed in degree zero.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] part (3) — `Stacks.Algebraization`
`.nonempty_iso_completion_limit_adicQuotientSystem`, which identifies `ℱ^∧` with the ordinary
limit `lim ℱ/ℐⁿℱ` — composed with part (4),
`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_single_limit_powerQuotients`, which says that the ordinary
limit is a derived limit of the tower. The existence of the product of the terms is produced by
part (4) and is quantified here as it is there.

The hypotheses are those of part (3): the ideal sheaf is
`Stacks.Algebraization.koszulIdealSheafData`, the extension to `Y` of the ideal the sections
`f_1, …, f_r` span, so its generation by them is a definition rather than a hypothesis, and
`[CompactSpace Y]` is the hypothesis the Artin–Rees level of part (3) consumes. No tag attribute
is attached: the statement is the conjunction of two of the tag's parts in another packaging, and
each of them carries its own registration where it is proved. -/
public theorem isDerivedLimit_adicQuotientSystem_completion :
    ∃ h : HasProduct (fun n : ℕ =>
        (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f) ℱ ⋙
          DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0).obj ⟨n⟩),
      @IsDerivedLimit (DerivedCategory Y.Modules) _ _ _ _ _ _
        (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f) ℱ ⋙
          DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0) h
        ((RingedSite.completionFunctor (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) f).obj
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (RingedSite.singleSheafComplex
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) ℱ))) := by
  obtain ⟨hprod, hlim₀⟩ :=
    isDerivedLimit_single_limit_powerQuotients (koszulIdealSheafData Y f) ℱ
  have : HasProduct (fun n : ℕ =>
      (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f) ℱ ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0).obj ⟨n⟩) := hprod
  have hlim : @IsDerivedLimit (DerivedCategory Y.Modules) _ _ _ _ _ _
      (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f) ℱ ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0) ‹_›
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor Y.Modules 0).obj
        (limit (adicQuotientSystem (koszulIdealSheafData Y f) ℱ))) := hlim₀
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_iso_completion_limit_adicQuotientSystem Y f ℱ
  exact ⟨‹_›, IsDerivedLimit.of_isoObj e.symm hlim⟩

end Main

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
